OL,3,GNEWSAFormer mining site could become
OL,4,Anature reserve
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former colliery site could become a
OL,7,Fnature reserve if powers are
OL,8,Ftransferred to a parish council.
OL,10,FThe mine at Shincliffe Pit Heaps, near
OL,11,FDurham, closed in 1886 and the site is
OL,12,Fnow home to several species, including
OL,13,Fthe increasingly rare Dingy Skipper
OL,14,Fbutterfly.
OL,16,FShincliffe Parish Council, which owns
OL,17,Fthe site, wants to create a nature
OL,18,Freserve there, but needs Durham County
OL,19,FCouncil to delegate its powers.
OL,21,FThe local authority is expected to make
OL,22,Fa decision later.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
